  "intent_snapshot": {
    "contract": "assurance_kernel/task_intent/v1",
    "task_id": "wc-batch-authorization-lifetime",
    "goal": "Make one Batch Authorization span the work it authorizes: derive its expiry from the authorized budget deadline on both Hosts instead of a hardcoded ten minutes, without relaxing any fail-closed clock, issuance, or renewal check.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "TTL-1",
        "assertion": "Batch authorization expiry is derived from the authorized budget.deadline_at on both Hosts, replacing the hardcoded now + 10 minutes in runtime/claude/kernel_ports.ts and .pi-extension/imm-unattended-batch.ts. The value bound at issuance is the one the literal user confirmed; no new default deadline is introduced and the existing default budget is unchanged.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v1\",\n  \"runner_id\": \"bun\",\n  \"runner_version\": \"1.4.2\",\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"test\",\n    \"tests/claude-batch-authority.test.ts\",\n    \"tests/pi-batch-authority.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \".\",\n  \"timeout_ms\": 120000,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 65536\n}\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "TTL-2",
        "assertion": "Every existing fail-closed check in runtime/kernel/batch_authority.ts is preserved verbatim in effect: expiry and deadline must both be strictly in the future at issuance, an unreadable or non-monotonic clock still fails closed, and an expired authorization still refuses the batch and still requires a strictly newer literal-user confirmation to renew.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v1\",\n  \"runner_id\": \"bun\",\n  \"runner_version\": \"1.4.2\",\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"test\",\n    \"tests/kernel-batch-authority.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \".\",\n  \"timeout_ms\": 60000,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 20000\n}\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "TTL-3",
        "assertion": "The renewal path in runtime/unattended/batch_runner.ts is retained, because a batch can still outlive a deadline the user themselves chose; a batch parked on a foreground Review inside its confirmed budget no longer expires, while one that passes its confirmed deadline still does.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v1\",\n  \"runner_id\": \"bun\",\n  \"runner_version\": \"1.4.2\",\n  \"argv\": [\n    \"test\",\n    \"tests/unattended-batch-run.test.ts\",\n    \"tests/dual-host-assurance-conformance.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"cwd\": \".\",\n  \"timeout_ms\": 120000,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 131072\n}\n"
      }
    ],
